>ENOMOTO TAKAYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HASHIMOTO KYOSUKE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KUBOKI NAOBUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIMOTO TAKUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKAMURA HIROYO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ENOMOTO, TAKAYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HASHIMOTO, KYOSUKE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUBOKI, NAOBUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIMOTO, TAKUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKAMURA, HIROYO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A pressure sensor in the form of film is provided, for instance, between the surface of a vehicle seat and a cushion material such as urethane. A sensor (20) in the form of film comprises an insulating film (21a, 21b), on which is formed a temperature detector (25) for detecting the temperature of a pressure detector (23). The temperature detector (25) is composed of a material whose electrical resistance varies with temperature. The temperature measured by the temperature detector (25) is used to reduce or eliminate measurement errors caused by varying temperature.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un capteur de pression se présentant sous forme d'un film et qui peut être placé, par exemple, entre la surface d'un siège de véhicule et un matériau de coussin tel que l'uréthane. Ce capteur (20) sous forme de film comprend un film isolant (21a, 21b) sur lequel est formé un détecteur (25) de température qui détecte la température du capteur (23) de pression. Ce détecteur (25) de température est constitué d'un matériau dont la résistance électrique varie avec la température. La température mesurée par le détecteur (25) est utilisée pour réduire ou éliminer les erreurs de mesure dues aux variations de température.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>